<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Pizarro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Pizarro was a Spanish conquistador who led the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>. In 1532 he captured the Inca ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cajamarca">Cajamarca</a> and later executed him, opening the way to Spanish control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and enormous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> wealth for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro.jpg" alt="Francisco Pizarro" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amable-Paul Coutan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Francisco_Pizarro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
